## 10. Real-World Telecom Application

Telecom systems generate large volumes of usage records, call-detail records, network activity, and customer events.

Chunk-based processing can be useful when:

* A CSV file is too large to comfortably load as one DataFrame.
* A batch ETL pipeline processes daily or monthly usage exports.
* Analysts need totals, counts, or other aggregations without retaining every row.
* Data is being prepared for later analysis in a database or data warehouse.

The same general idea of processing data in partitions is also relevant to distributed processing frameworks such as Apache Spark and Hadoop. However, pandas chunk processing runs within a single Python process and is not itself distributed computing.

## 11. Conclusion

This exercise demonstrated how to process a large simulated telecom dataset using pandas chunk-based reading. By reading 100,000 rows at a time and maintaining running totals, the program calculates total data usage and counts high-usage records without creating one full-size DataFrame during the analysis stage.
